    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold;">Feeder protection and control / Feeder protection</h1>
            <div style="text-align: right;">
                <span data-field="document_id">{{ document_id }}</span><br>
                <span data-field="revision">{{ revision }}</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 30px;">Product version: <span data-field="product_version">{{ product_version }}</span></p>

        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">7. Measurement</h2>
            <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">8. Event log</h2>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The relay continuously measures phase currents and earth currents. Earth current can be measured using external core balance current transformer or can be calculated internally.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">During service, the default view of display shows the measured phase currents in primary terms (Amps) and the earth current. The values measured can be accessed locally via the user interface on the relay or remotely via the communication interface of the relay.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The relay continuously measures negative sequence current, thermal level and counter values if these functions are supported as per application configurations.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">To collect sequence of - events (SoE) information, the relay incorporates a non-volatile memory with a capacity of storing 100 events with associated time stamps with resolution of 1 ms. Event log includes trip circuit supervision status and relay fault code. The event log data is stored sequentially, the most recent being first, and the oldest event is overwritten. This data also in case the relay temporarily loses its auxiliary supply.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The event log facilitates detailed post-fault analysis of feeder faults and disturbances. The SoE information can be accessed locally via the user interface on the relay front panel or remotely via the communication interface of the relay.</p>
    </div>

