        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">9. Recorded data</h2>
            <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">10. Self-supervision and test function</h2>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The relay stores fault records of analogue values for the last five trip events in non-volatile memory.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The fault recording is triggered by the trip signal and stores the measured values of all measured quantities at the current value for three phases and earth current.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The recorded data can be accessed locally via the user interface on the relay front panel and can be uploaded for subsequent fault analysis.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The relay's built-in self-supervision system continuously monitors the state of the relay hardware and the operation of the relay software.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The self-supervision system checks the internal hardware and software integrity, and reports any faults to the user via the relay's front panel or via the communication interface.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The relay also has a test mode which enables user to test the relay HMI and binary outputs.</p>

        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">11. Trip-circuit supervision</h2>
            <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">12. Access control</h2>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The trip-circuit supervision continuously monitors the availability and operability of the trip circuit.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">It provides open-circuit monitoring both when the circuit breaker is in its closed and in its open position. It also detects loss of circuit-breaker control voltage.</p>

        <p style="font-size: 11pt;">To protect the relay from unauthorized access, the relay is equipped with a password protection system with individual password.</p>
    </div>

